course: dictionary
lesson: 9344
title: Spirited: full of life and courage
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word spirited is an adjective. It describes someone or something that is full of energy, courage and liveliness. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «a spirited little pony» is a pony with plenty of energy, one that tosses its head and will not stand still.
explain: Spirited can also describe an effort. «The team made a spirited effort, even though they lost.» The team lost, but the words "even though" show that they tried hard and played with courage. A spirited effort is a brave and lively one, even if it does not win.
explain: Spirited is also the past form of the verb spirit, as in "spirited away". Look at the clues: taken away quickly and secretly, as if by magic. Ask yourself what word would fit in the sentence, then swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
explain: In words like high-spirited, mean-spirited and public-spirited, the word tells you about someone's mood or heart. Public-spirited means someone cares about helping other people in the community.
fact: Spirited means full of energy, courage and liveliness.
fact: A spirited effort is brave and lively, even if it does not win.
fact: «Spirited away» means taken away quickly and secretly, as if by magic.
fact: Spirited is also the past form of the verb spirit.
fact: Phrases you may meet include high-spirited, free-spirited, mean-spirited, public-spirited and a spirited debate.
exercise: «The spirited little pony tossed its head and would not stand still.» What does spirited mean? | Very small and quiet | Lost and afraid | Sleepy and calm | *Full of energy and liveliness
exercise: «The team made a spirited effort, even though they lost.» What does a spirited effort show? | Tired and hungry | Careless and lazy | *Brave, lively trying | Quiet and sad
exercise: In the phrase «spirited away», which meaning fits? | *Taken away quickly and secretly, as if by magic | Shouted at loudly | Sent away with a letter | Painted in bright colours
test: «The debate was spirited, with everyone speaking up.» What does spirited suggest here? | Boring and slow | Quiet and gloomy | Cancelled | *Lively and full of energy
test: What does public-spirited tell you about someone? | They do not like other people | They are always tired | They are very tall | *They care about helping the community
exam: Alice feels «very lonely and low-spirited» and cries. In this sentence, what does low-spirited mean? | Full of energy | Lost in a forest | Very tall | *Sad
